-- Playbook ve-pricing-points-passport: Earn your Passport build record, parts 1 and 2 (Logan, 2026-11-01). Safe to run twice.
insert into public.playbook_records (slug, brand_slug, author, body, source, kind)
select 've-pricing-points-passport', 'vegans-explore', 'Logan', $pb$BUILD RECORD, 2026-11-01 (Logan). Earn your Passport, parts 1 and 2 built and live (Sean: "Logan, build it").
1. THE CHECK-IN MENU. After I'm here: What I ordered and I bought something (a photo, only while the check-in is open, 3 hours), Post it (an Instagram or TikTok link), a shout-out (positive prompt), and the bounties open at that place. One of each per check-in; every one waits in Depot > Check-ins; approving pays 15, 25, 25 or 10 points; an approved shout-out shows on the listing under What members say. Owners earn nothing at their own place. Migration 20261101_checkin_actions.sql, ve-checkin from commit 8ce1037 (sha256 matched).
2. PASSPORT CHALLENGE STOPS, CARDS AND THE VAULT. /business/challenge: the offer, the card as it looks on a phone, the agreement (typed name, a 4 to 6 digit staff PIN, I agree; the account is made at the button), sent. South Florida only for the pilot. Depot > Passport Challenge stops: pick up to five a chapter a month by the 10th; picking makes the business a member (Founding before January 1), covers its claim, and makes four $25 cards that open on the 1st with a week's bidding. /vault: cards by chapter, bidding for members (at least 100 points, never on your own place's cards), Your cards with Use this card (staff type the PIN, used once), and the stops. Settled every 15 minutes: the highest eligible bid wins, one win a month, only the winner's points are taken, cards good for 12 months. The Vegan Restaurant Guide's Promotions has Be a Passport Challenge stop. Migrations 20261101_passport_challenge_stops_vault.sql and 20261101_vault_owner_no_bid.sql, ve-vault from commit 3ea6ed1 (sha256 matched).
PROVEN live on Love Life Cafe with the Logan test account and Sean's account, then every test row removed and Love Life Cafe put back unclaimed.
NEXT: 3. the Taster account and the sampler, 4. the three challenges, 5. the two-day business follow-up and the not-ready-yet emails, 6. the content gig, 7. the business points rule.$pb$, 'text', 'decision'
where not exists (select 1 from public.playbook_records where slug = 've-pricing-points-passport' and body like 'BUILD RECORD, 2026-11-01 (Logan). Earn your Passport, parts 1 and 2%');
